        // record C's owner by reading via low-level: owner is not public, so observe effect via balance trick
        // Instead, we rely on that constructor set owner=msg.sender and owner is used nowhere else; to observe change
        // we use a call that will revert when not owner: craft calldata that calls a function only owner can call.
        // But C has no such function. So instead we observe that delegatecall can modify C's storage; we'll detect that by
